[Music]  welcome back to cbs mornings we're at a  crucial moment in the crisis over  ukraine the president met with his  national security team over the weekend  and vice president harris spoke with  ukraine's president in germany u.s  intelligence believes the kremlin has  now given russian troops orders to  proceed mr biden has agreed to meet with  president putin if russia does not  invade we're joined now by president  biden's national security adviser jake  sullivan jake good morning  good morning  so as you know president biden met with  his national security council yesterday  you were in that meeting can you share  with us the results  well president biden convened that  meeting in order to prepare a response  should russia  actually move forward and invade ukraine  and he's been clear all along throughout  this crisis that the united states and  its allies are ready either way we're  ready to continue diplomacy including at  the highest levels to try to resolve  this matter peacefully but we are  equally ready and we are united as the  west in imposing swift and severe  consequences if russia chooses to move  forward  and yesterday president biden got a  briefing on the details and the final  plans for those consequences should  russia move in the coming hours or days  yesterday on face the nation jake the  russian ambassador said listen there are  no such plans for an invasion which is  so confusing because you know when  you're a little kid and they say if it  walks like a duck sounds like a duck  looks like a duck it's a duck it seems  like we're just waiting for something to  happen can we be more proactive here  well first we have been very proactive  in laying out for the world precisely  what russia's plans and intentions are  and how they intend to put them into  motion and last week at the u.n security  council secretary blinken spoke to the  world and he warned the world that  russia would try to manufacture a crisis  in the conflict-stricken portions of  eastern ukraine that's exactly what  happened over the weekend he warned that  the russians would then make a show of  big meetings in moscow and in fact  that's exactly what's happening today  with president putin convening his  national security council so what we  have done is indicate to the world that  this is not something russia has been  provoked into this is a brutal war of  choice  that russia will be perpetrating on its  neighbor and that will enable enable us  if they in fact do move forward to rally  not just the west but the world to hold  russia accountable for what it has done  and then finally in terms of being  proactive we have moved thousands of u.s  troops to poland and romania and other  parts of europe in order to ensure that  every inch of nato territory is defended  against any further russian aggression  that goes beyond ukraine  jake the president said the military  will not help evacuate americans from  russia or ukraine what is the biden  administration doing  to help ensure that americans can leave  those countries safely and quickly if  needed  well part of the reason we went out  early and very clearly and said to  american citizens in ukraine it's time  to leave now  is to give them as much opportunity to  take advantage of commercial options air  and rail and road to get out of ukraine  to get home or to get to other parts of  europe more than 10 days ago  we indicated to them that they should  leave in the next 24 to 48 hours we have  continued to say that every single day  and we hope that americans will make the  responsible choice  and jake before you go can you help the  american people understand why we should  be concerned about this this country  people are looking at covert they're  looking at rising prices they're looking  at you know the gas is high the food is  high why should we be  why should we pay close attention to  this why does this matter to us  we have seen before how a small war in  europe can grow if we don't stand up in  strong and resolute terms to defend our  allies and partners that's why president  biden has sent troops to nato territory  not to fight russia and ukraine but to  defend nato and that has helped keep the  peace over the course of the past seven  decades in europe kept a major power war  between the u.s and russia from  happening i think it matters and it's  the basic value of freedom of choice and  freedom of destiny for all people  everywhere that's deep in the american  dna and that's why we support the  ukrainian people in this time  all right national security advisor jake  sullivan thank you so much we appreciate  you

